171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T (For decades, organizational transformation and long-term sustainability have been approached primarily through technology, processes, and organizational structures. Companies have in vested billions in implementing new systems, redefining strategies, redesigning organizational structures, and launching large-scale transformation initiatives. Yet research consistently shows that the majority of these initiatives fail to achieve their intended outcomes.)
/E (For decades, organizational transformation and long-term sustainability have been approached primarily through technology, processes, and organizational structures. Companies have in vested billions in implementing new systems, redefining strategies, redesigning organizational structures, and launching large-scale transformation initiatives. Yet research consistently shows that the majority of these initiatives fail to achieve their intended outcomes.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T (The fundamental reason is that organizations often assume that redesigning processes will naturally lead to changes in human behavior. In reality, what changes is not the process itself, but the decisions people make within it, their habits, learning patterns, collaborative behaviors, and responses to change. Behavior is not merely the outcome of management practices; it is rooted in the biological and cognitive principles that govern the human brain.)
/E (The fundamental reason is that organizations often assume that redesigning processes will naturally lead to changes in human behavior. In reality, what changes is not the process itself, but the decisions people make within it, their habits, learning patterns, collaborative behaviors, and responses to change. Behavior is not merely the outcome of management practices; it is rooted in the biological and cognitive principles that govern the human brain.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T <>
/E <>
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
