/T (Behavior, however, does not emerge spontaneously. It is shaped by the brain's threat and reward systems, habit loops, social networks, identity structures, and cognitive capacity. These systems are, in turn, influenced by the architecture of the organization itself. This scientific understanding marks the starting point of a new paradigm: organizational behavior must be intentionally designed, not simply expected to emerge.)
/E (Behavior, however, does not emerge spontaneously. It is shaped by the brain's threat and reward systems, habit loops, social networks, identity structures, and cognitive capacity. These systems are, in turn, influenced by the architecture of the organization itself. This scientific understanding marks the starting point of a new paradigm: organizational behavior must be intentionally designed, not simply expected to emerge.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
