254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (We design organizations by starting with the neurobiological mechanisms that govern human decision-making, learning, adaptation, and behavior. Rather than treating AI, Human Resources, leadership, and sustainability as separate disciplines, we integrate them into a single organizational nervous system. In doing so, we help organizations build sustainable organizational intelligence and create a new operating system for the future of work.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (It is increasingly difficult to talk about the future of leadership, talent, human resources, or long-term organizational sustainability without accounting for the neurobiological limits, capacities, and operating principles of the human brain. Our approach is built entirely around these realities.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Technology has never been the real challenge. The challenge is that human behavior and system design rarely speak the same language. The only way to unlock the full value of technological algorithms is to first understand the algorithms of the human brain. That is why neuroscience-based approaches are becoming essential for organizational transformation.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
