/Title (As a result, organizational sustainability and transformation are entering a new era. The competitive advantage of the future will not come merely from adopting the latest technologies, but from designing organizational systems that align with how people think, learn, make decisions, and adapt. It requires a scientific understanding of how organizational environments shape behavior and the ability to intentionally design systems based on that knowledge. This perspective views organizations not simply as structures for managing processes, but as living systems in which decisions, habits, attention, learning, and collaboration are continuously shaped and reinforced.)
